<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Aerodynamics. ALL COEFFICIENTS ARE PLACEHOLDERS for a generic straight-wing aircraft (aspect
  ratio 6.4) with a 35 deg V-tail; replace them with XFLR5 results (see the aircraft modeling
  plan on the aircraft-modeling branch). Each term says how its number was set.

  Forces are in wind axes (LIFT, DRAG, SIDE); moments in stability axes, the frame XFLR5 gives
  its derivatives in, about AERORP (= the nominal CG). Rates are normalised the usual way:
  p and r by b/2V (aero/bi2vel), q and alpha-dot by c/2V (aero/ci2vel).

  Surfaces: +rad = trailing edge down (FlightControl.xml). Each surface is its own term, so one
  surface failing or moving the wrong way affects the flight the way it would on the aircraft.
  V-tail panels: each panel's normal force is 0.175/rad of deflection (panel area 0.04 m2 / wing
  area 0.40 m2 x lift slope 3.5/rad x flap effectiveness 0.5), split by the 35 deg dihedral into
  lift (cos 35 = 0.819) and side force (sin 35 = 0.574), acting 0.55 m behind the CG.

  scale/* (FlightControl.xml) multiply the terms the tuning sweeps vary; all 1 by default.
-->
